{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-106602-r4630340","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Montreal Russian Borscht","sourcePageId":106602,"sourceRevision":"4630340","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2026-04-12T21:23:59Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Montreal%20Russian%20Borscht&oldid=4630340","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T13:09:19.205Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Canadian recipes","Category:Easy recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for borscht","Category:Recipes for soup","Category:Recipes using beet","Category:Recipes using carrot","Category:Recipes using garlic","Category:Recipes using green cabbage","Category:Recipes using sugar","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Recipes without servings","Category:Russian recipes","Category:Vegan recipes"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"d37cab9588902f7651c4e8aa1409266817d16606fd04071b652666a96d1794d6","sourceWikitext":"{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Soup recipes\n| Difficulty = 2\n}}\n\n{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Cuisine of Russia|Cuisine of Russia]] | [[Cookbook:Soups|Soups]]\n\n'''Montreal Russian borscht''' was a prize winner in Montreal, Canada's Russian community\n\n==Ingredients==\n* 7 [[Cookbook:Liter|litres]] [[Cookbook:water|water]]\n* 1 can stewed [[Cookbook:tomato|tomato]]es, or an equivalent amount of fresh tomatoes\n* 1 small can [[Cookbook:Tomato Paste|tomato paste]]\n* [[cookbook:sugar|Sugar]] to taste\n* [[cookbook:salt|Salt]], to taste\n* 1 large [[cookbook:onion|onion]], thinly [[Cookbook:Slicing|sliced]]\n* 1–2 cloves [[cookbook:garlic|garlic]]\n* 5–6 medium [[cookbook:beet|beet]]s, peeled and [[Cookbook:Julienne|julienned]]\n* 3 medium [[cookbook:carrot|carrot]]s, peeled and julienned\n* 1 [[cookbook:potato|potato]], julienned (optional)\n* &frac12; large [[cookbook:Cabbage|white cabbage]], shredded \n\n==Procedure==\n# Fill large [[cookbook:stock pot|stock pot]] with water. Add can stewed tomatoes, tomato paste, sugar, salt, onion, garlic, and beets, and [[cookbook:boil|boil]] for 20 minutes.                       \n# Add carrots, cabbage, and potato.\n# Return to a boil and cook for 1.5 hours\n\n==Notes, tips, and variations==\n\n* It's very important to remember that this particular recipe is somewhat like wine. The older it gets, the better it gets. It is recommended to let sit in refrigerator for at least two days, before serving. The difference is truly remarkable.\n\n[[Category:Recipes for soup]]\n[[Category:Vegan recipes]]\n[[Category:Russian recipes]]\n[[Category:Canadian recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes for borscht]]\n[[Category:Recipes using beet]]\n[[Category:Recipes using green cabbage]]\n[[Category:Recipes using sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using carrot]]\n[[Category:Recipes using garlic]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Montreal Russian Borscht","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"7 litres water","sourceText":"7 litres water","amountText":"7 litres water","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"1 can stewed tomatoes, or an equivalent amount of fresh tomatoes","sourceText":"1 can stewed tomatoes, or an equivalent amount of fresh tomatoes","amountText":